[68.78691, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m2\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠹\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[68.787493, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe input uses ISO timestamps with fractional seconds, which jq 1.6’s `fromdateiso8601` does not parse directly. I’ll verify a normalized-date filter before \r\nwriting the final files.\r\n\r\n```\r\nset -e\r\nprintf '%s\\n' '--- fromdate direct ---'\r\njq -n '\"2026-03-30T15:06:40.723617Z\" | fromdateiso8601' 2>&1 || true\r\nprintf '%s\\n' '--- normalized fromdate ---'\r\njq -n '\"2026-03-30T15:06:40.723617Z\" | sub(\"\\\\.[0-9]+Z$\"; \"Z\") | fromdateiso8601 | strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")'\r\nprintf '%s\\n' '--- prefix ---'"]
[68.787503, "o", "\r\njq -n '\"2026-03-30T15:06:40.723617Z\" | .[0:10]'\r\nprintf '%s\\n' '--- yq type ---'\r\ncommand -v yq; head -40 \"$(command -v yq)\" 2>/dev/null || true\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠹\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[68.787967, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠹\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
