[93.537332, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe reconstructed command produced a byte-identical report; my validation jq expression itself was malformed because it compared against `inputs`. I’ll rerun \r\nthe checks with correct jq expressions.\r\n\r\n```\r\nset -e\r\ncd /app\r\n# Validate output structure, date format, field names, and ascending username sort\r\njq -e '\r\n  (type == \"array\") and\r\n  (all(.[]; (keys | sort) == [\"email\",\"last_login\",\"primary_role\",\"role_count\",\"user_id\",\"username\"])) and\r\n  (all(.[]; (.last_login | test(\"^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$\")))) and\r\n  (all(.[]; (.user_id | type) == \"number\")) and\r\n  (all(.[]; (.role_count | type) == \"number\")) and\r\n  ([.[].username] == ([.[].username] | sort))\r\n' /app/active_users_report.json >/dev/null\r\necho 'schema/date/sort: valid'\r\n# Validate active filtering and role-related fields against source data\r\njq -e --slurpfile report /app/active_users_report.json '\r\n  ([.[] | select(.status == \"active\")] | length) == ($report[0] | length) and\r\n  ([.[] | select(.status == \"active\" and (.roles | length) ="]
[93.537374, "o", "= 0)] | length) ==\r\n   ([$report[0][] | select(.primary_role == null)] | length) and\r\n  all($report[0][]; .role_count >= 0)\r\n' /app/users.json >/dev/null\r\necho 'source consistency: valid'\r\n# Show counts and YAML key count/argument values\r\necho \"active source users: $(jq '[.[] | select(.status == \"active\")] | length' /app/users.json)\"\r\necho \"report users: $(jq 'length' /app/active_users_report.json)\"\r\necho \"YAML top-level keys: $(yq -r 'keys | join(\", \")' /app/jq_args.yaml)\"\r\nprintf 'YAML args:\\n'; yq -r '.args[]' /app/jq_args.yaml\r\n# Confirm indentation is exactly two spaces for first object field\r\nsed -n '2p' /app/active_users_report.json | cat -A\r\necho 'all checks passed'\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠇\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠇\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
