[100.543484, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe main validations pass. I’ll do one final field-level cross-check against the source to ensure every transformed value corresponds to the correct active \r\nuser, then submit.\r\n\r\n```\r\nset -e\r\ncd /app\r\njq -e --slurpfile report /app/active_users_report.json '\r\n  ($report[0]) as $r |\r\n  ([.[] | select(.status == \"active\")] | length) == ($r | length) and\r\n  ([.[] | select(.status == \"active\") | .id] | sort) == ([$r[].user_id] | sort) and\r\n  all($r[] as $out;\r\n    (.[] | select(.id == $out.user_id)) as $src |\r\n    $src.status == \"active\" and\r\n    $out.username == $src.username and\r\n    $out.email == $src.email and\r\n    $out.last_login == ($src.last_login[0:10]) and\r\n    $out.role_count == ($src.roles | length) and\r\n    ($out.primary_role == ($src.roles[0] // null))\r\n  )\r\n' /app/users.json >/dev/null\r\necho 'field-level source comparison: valid'\r\nls -l /app/users.json /app/active_users_report.json /app/cmd.sh /app/jq_args.yaml\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠸\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[100.544387, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠸\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[100.559566, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mTool\u001b[0m:\r\n"]
