[105.497429, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m7\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠋\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[105.49794, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe field-level checker hit a jq syntax error in the `all(... as ...)` form. I’ll correct it to use `all(generator; condition)` with proper variable binding.\r\n\r\n```\r\nset -e\r\ncd /app\r\njq -e --slurpfile report /app/active_users_report.json '\r\n  . as $users |\r\n  $report[0] as $r |\r\n  (([$users[] | select(.status == \"active\")] | length) == ($r | length)) and\r\n  (([$users[] | select(.status == \"active\") | .id] | sort) == ([$r[].user_id] | sort)) and\r\n  all($r[];\r\n    . as $out |\r\n    ($users[] | select(.id == $out.user_id)) as $src |\r\n    $src.status == \"active\" and\r\n    $out.username == $src.username and\r\n    $out.email == $src.email and\r\n    $out.last_login == ($src.last_login[0:10]) and\r\n    $out.role_count == ($src.roles | length) and\r\n    ($out.primary_role == ($src.roles[0] // null))\r\n  )\r\n' /app/users.json >/dev/null\r\necho 'field-level source comparison: valid'\r\nls -l /app/users.json /app/active_users_report.json /app/cmd.sh /app/jq_args.yaml\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠋\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[105.498142, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠋\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[105.600708, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mTool\u001b[0m:\r\n"]
